        "text": "Let's calculate. A spacecraft is one hundred metres long at rest, and passes a space station at zero point eight c. What length does the station measure? Gamma at zero point eight c is one point six seven, so l is one hundred over one point six seven, sixty metres. Its height, at right angles to the motion, is unchanged. And on board, the ship is still one hundred metres long."
      },
      "durationInFrames": 1,
      "holdSeconds": 0,
      "holdKind": "visual"
    },
